<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-01-12T06:49:14+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Mon, 12 Jan 2026 06:49:14 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[Signal to attack Iran? Trump posts mysterious 'soon' photo and the internet goes crazy]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/126470980.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Former President Donald Trump posted a cryptic 90s-style black-and-white image on Truth Social with the single word "soon." The unexplained image, showing Trump atop the White House, sparked widespread speculation among supporters and critics alike. While some Republicans interpreted it as a hint of future military or political action, others mocked the post as nonsensical or AI-generated.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/etimes/trending/signal-to-attack-iran-trump-posts-mysterious-soon-photo-and-the-internet-goes-crazy/articleshow/126470980.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/etimes/trending/signal-to-attack-iran-trump-posts-mysterious-soon-photo-and-the-internet-goes-crazy/articleshow/126470980.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-01-12T02:43:58+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Trending Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-126470989,imgsize-565002.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[MAGA ‘turns on’ Kristi Noem? Trump allies uneasy over ‘highly problematic’ handling of ICE shooting]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/126467379.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Governor Kristi Noem's swift labeling of Renee Good's death as 'domestic terrorism' is causing unease, even within MAGA circles.  Critics and allies alike question the premature pronouncements amid ongoing investigations.  The administration's firm stance, echoed by Trump and Vance, faces scrutiny as video evidence sparks divided interpretations, raising concerns about public trust and political fallout.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/maga-turns-on-kristi-noem-trump-allies-uneasy-over-highly-problematic-handling-of-ice-shooting/articleshow/126467379.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/maga-turns-on-kristi-noem-trump-allies-uneasy-over-highly-problematic-handling-of-ice-shooting/articleshow/126467379.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-01-11T21:26:43+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-126467397,imgsize-33316.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[From Jeff Bezos to Bill Gates: Billionaires bet on Greenland as Trump hints at taking it ‘the hard way’]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/126470878.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Donald Trump's renewed interest in acquiring Greenland, framed as a national security issue, coincides with significant investments by prominent businessmen like Ronald Lauder. Tech billionaires Jeff Bezos and Bill Gates, through KoBold Metals, are also exploring the island for rare earth minerals, raising questions about strategic influence and growing American presence.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/from-jeff-bezos-to-bill-gates-billionaires-bet-on-greenland-as-trump-hints-at-taking-it-the-hard-way/articleshow/126470878.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/from-jeff-bezos-to-bill-gates-billionaires-bet-on-greenland-as-trump-hints-at-taking-it-the-hard-way/articleshow/126470878.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-01-12T01:49:59+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-126470888,imgsize-48816.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Ilhan Omar asks why ICE agent Jonathan Ross was in front of Renee Good's moving car in Minneapolis]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/126470924.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/ilhan-omar-asks-why-ice-agent-jonathan-ross-was-in-front-of-renee-goods-moving-car-in-minneapolis/articleshow/126470924.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/ilhan-omar-asks-why-ice-agent-jonathan-ross-was-in-front-of-renee-goods-moving-car-in-minneapolis/articleshow/126470924.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-01-12T02:05:59+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static